Q: Creating a fixed length output string with sprintf containing floats A: <p>Just write a binary file, where the sign bit isn't a concern.</p>
<p>An added benefit is that (in general) you'll be writing 12 bytes vs. 32 for each item (a green solution :-). After all, you lose precision when doing a sprintf and an <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atof#Numeric_conversions" rel="nofollow noreferrer">atof</a> on the other side.</p>
<p>If this isn't viable,</p>
<pre><code>int len_lng = lng &lt; 0 ? 6: 7;
int len_lat = lat &lt; 0 ? 6: 7;
char fmt[128];
sprintf(fmt, &quot;%%10i %%3.%df %%3.%df\n&quot;, len_lng, len_lat);
sprintf(osm_node_repr, fmt, node-&gt;id, node-&gt;lng, node-&gt;lat);
</code></pre>
